# This is the processing directive for uni-temporal Anchor Modeling in PostgreSQL
#
# The templates are in the Sisula language (docs/SISULA.md) and render the JSON bindings that the
# modeler builds (Generate > JSON bindings). The scripts first in the list prepare the schema that the
# bindings are made from; they run once, before the templates. A line starting with # is not run.
SQL/Helpers.js
SQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/PostgreSQL/NamingConvention.js
SQL/PostgreSQL/derive.js
SQL/PostgreSQL/CreateSchemas.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateEquivalentAndDefault.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateKnots.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateAnchors.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateNexuses.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateAttributes.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateTies.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateKnotEquivalenceViews.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateAttributeEquivalenceViews.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateAttributeRewinders.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateAnchorPerspectives.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateNexusPerspectives.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/uni/CreateTiePerspectives.sisula
SQL/PostgreSQL/AddDescriptions.sisula
